{"id":"trespass-offering","name":"Trespass Offering","aliases":[],"sources":["torrey","easton"],"topics":["torrey:trespass-offering"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Trespass offering","text":"(Heb. ‘asham, “debt”), the law concerning, given in Lev. 5:14-6:7; also in Num. 5:5-8. The idea of sin as a “debt” pervades this legislation. The asham, which was always a ram, was offered in cases where sins were more private. (See OFFERING.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H817","lemma":"אָשָׁם","xlit":"ʼâshâm","gloss":"guilt","kjv":"guiltiness, sin, trespass","count":18,"share":0.41},{"strong":"H2403","lemma":"חַטָּאָה","xlit":"chaṭṭâʼâh","gloss":"an offence , and its penalty, occasion, sacrifice, or ex","kjv":"punishment, purifying, sin","count":17,"share":0.39},{"strong":"H2398","lemma":"חָטָא","xlit":"châṭâʼ","gloss":"to miss","kjv":"bear the blame, cleanse, commit, by fault","count":14,"share":0.32},{"strong":"H3722","lemma":"כָּפַר","xlit":"kâphar","gloss":"to cover","kjv":"appease, make, put off, reconcile","count":11,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H816","lemma":"אָשַׁם","xlit":"ʼâsham","gloss":"to be guilty","kjv":"certainly, be desolate, destroy, greatly","count":7,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H8449","lemma":"תּוֹר","xlit":"tôwr","gloss":"a ring-dove, often as a term of endearment","kjv":"dove","count":6,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Lev.5.6","Lev.5.7","Lev.5.15","Lev.5.16","Lev.5.18","Lev.5.19","Lev.6.6","Lev.14.12","Lev.14.13","Lev.14.14","Lev.14.21","Lev.19.21","Lev.19.22","Num.6.12","Isa.53.10","Ezek.40.39","Ezek.44.29","Ezek.46.20","Lev.4.1","Lev.5.1","Lev.5.2","Lev.5.3","Lev.5.4","Lev.5.5","Lev.5.8","Lev.5.9","Lev.5.10","Lev.5.11","Lev.5.12","Lev.5.13","Lev.5.17","Lev.6.2","Lev.6.3","Lev.6.4","Lev.6.5","Lev.6.7","Lev.12.6","Lev.12.7","Lev.12.8","Lev.14.2","Lev.14.22","Lev.15.14","Lev.15.15","Lev.19.20"],"related":[{"id":"dove-turtle","type":"cooccur","shared":7,"jaccard":0.111,"why":"7 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"perjury","type":"cooccur","shared":6,"j